      "code_hash": "1a4a4bf35fea243545119e4225fbca45",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"3-a-loop-you-can-bend\">3. A loop you can bend</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The pad below is <a href=\"https://github.com/koaning/wigglystuff\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">wigglystuff</a>'s\n<code>CurveEditor</code>, turned into a loop. Drag its knots, double-click to add or remove one,\nor roll the \ud83c\udfb2. A dot rides the loop in time with the music, once around per loop\n(drag the <code>1\u00d7</code> for more laps).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The stack below the pad can follow the dot:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>in a layer</th>\n<th>what it is</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>path.x</code></td>\n<td>how far right the dot is, 0 to 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>path.y</code></td>\n<td>how high the dot is, 0 to 1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>path.knots</code></td>\n<td>a hit each time the dot passes a knot</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Here the dot's height plays a melody, its left-right position opens a filter and pans\nthe hats, and every knot is a rim shot. Press \u25b6 on the player, then reshape the loop.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
